---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../../components/CardGrid.astro';
import DocCard from '../../../components/DocCard.astro';
const sidebar = [
  { title: 'Documentation Home', href: '/docs' },
  { title: 'Reference Overview', href: '/docs/reference' },
  { title: 'Glossary', href: '/docs/reference/glossary' },
  { title: 'Known Issues', href: '/docs/reference/known-issues' },
  { title: 'Roadmap', href: '/docs/reference/roadmap' },
  { title: 'Changelog', href: '/docs/reference/changelog', active: true },
  { title: 'Literature', href: '/docs/reference/literature' },
];
const toc = [
  { id: 'unreleased', text: 'Unreleased', level: 2 },
  { id: 'historical', text: 'Historical', level: 2 },
  { id: 'versioning', text: 'Versioning', level: 2 },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Changelog" description="History of changes to the system" section="Reference" sidebar={sidebar} toc={toc}>
  <CardGrid columns={3}>
    <DocCard title="Detection" href="#historical" icon="radar" tag="Pipeline" description="Pure module extraction, eve.json migration, shared decay policy and sophistication classification." meta="Rules" />
    <DocCard title="Routing & pooling" href="#historical" icon="route" tag="Edge" description="Twelve-stage decision pipeline, atomic pool assignment, score accumulation and escalation-aware decay." meta="Sessions" />
    <DocCard title="Security fixes" href="#historical" icon="shield" tag="Fixes" description="Header gating, plugin slug escaping, ngx.null handling, empty-array encoding and private-IP filtering." meta="Hardening" />
  </CardGrid>

  <h2 id="unreleased">Unreleased</h2>
  <h3>Features</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Pool autoscaling — the pool manager builds runtime pools per waiting session plus spares within a memory / CPU / count budget, and retires idle pools after <code>POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS</code>.</li>
    <li>Consent-gated device signature — a one-way <code>gdpr_signature</code> re-recognises a returning visitor after a cookie and storage wipe without storing any PII (<code>gdpr_handler.lua</code>, <code>GET /__gdpr/config</code>). See <a href="/docs/detection/signature">Device &amp; GDPR Signature</a>.</li>
    <li>Database-proxy honeypot layer — an alternative, lighter deception layer (<code>docker-compose.db-proxy.yml</code>) that swaps the database per request via <code>wp-content/db.php</code> instead of running separate decoy backends. See <a href="/docs/engine/layers">Honeypot Layers</a>.</li>
    <li>Generated pattern catalogue — one machine-readable <code>patterns/patterns.json</code> now feeds both the dashboard Pattern Database and the <a href="/docs/detection/patterns">documentation</a>, so the two cannot drift.</li>
    <li>Honeypot threshold raised from 50 to 80 to cut false positives on aggressive but legitimate REST API clients.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Documentation &amp; Tooling</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Documentation expansion for detection, observability, operations, testing, and reference sections — enriched with Lua code comments and architecture details.</li>
    <li>Astro knowledge hub with mkdocs-material styling, full-text search, section navigation, table of contents and documentation cards.</li>
    <li>New pages: Honeypot Layers, Device &amp; GDPR Signature; enriched reference (known issues, roadmap, literature) and the blind-pentest evaluation write-up with Run&nbsp;1 results.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Security</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><code>X-Route-Target</code> / <code>X-Risk-Score</code> response headers gated behind <code>INTERNAL_TEST_SECRET</code> (fail closed) after the blind pentest found they leaked a live routing/score oracle to the client.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="historical">Historical</h2>
  <h3>Detection Pipeline</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>pattern_analyzer.lua split into pure pattern_rules.lua + adapter.</li>
    <li>suricata_rules.lua migrated from fast.log regex to structured eve.json JSON parsing.</li>
    <li>vulnerability_rules.lua, abuseipdb_rules.lua, router_rules.lua, upload_rules.lua, admin_rules.lua, session_rules.lua extracted as pure modules.</li>
    <li>decay_policy.lua extracted as shared escalation-aware decay module.</li>
    <li>lua_pattern_utils.lua promoted from duplicated copies (fixing hyphen-escaping bug).</li>
    <li>sophistication_analyzer.lua added for scripted/ai_assisted/manual/unknown classification.</li>
    <li>honeytoken_handler.lua added for honeytoken injection and detection.</li>
    <li>gdpr_rules.lua / gdpr_handler.lua added for consent-gated privacy-preserving identity.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Routing & Pooling</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>router.lua decision pipeline with 12 stages.</li>
    <li>pool_router.lua implemented with exclusive assignment, spare provisioning, scale-up, reuse at resource limit.</li>
    <li>Score accumulation added (fixing session score laundering bug).</li>
    <li>Decay system added with offense-scaled half-life and permaflag thresholds.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Security Fixes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>admin-ajax.php excluded from is_admin_access() — fixed false-positive escalation.</li>
    <li>is_vulnerable_plugin_request() hyphen-escaping bug fixed.</li>
    <li>ngx.null sentinel crash fixed.</li>
    <li>Empty Lua tables tagged with cjson.empty_array_mt to prevent Elasticsearch mapping conflicts.</li>
    <li>Suricata private IP filtering added.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="versioning">Versioning</h2>
  <p>Changes are tracked with semantic versioning for engine, detection, and dashboard components.</p>
</DocsLayout>
